🔥💥Update: E-E-A-T-Signals Infographic👇

Since 2015, I have been researching measurable signals for the E-E-A-T quality or brand framework.

I have been able to find most of the possible signals via (Google) patents and other publications by Google.

Here are some of them: https://lnkd.in/gGXUBrcK

Since 2022, I have been publishing this updated infographic annually to give you an overview of what Google could use for quality classifiers in terms of E-E-A-T.

The following signals have been added:

Source Entity Level:
📍Total number of articles the author has written 
📍Amount of the author's articles are considered "evergreen" 
📍Average length of the author's content  

Document Level: 
📍Anchor text n-grams 
📍Steady stream of incoming links long after publication

Domain Level: 
📍Similarity to authoritative seed websites known for exceptional content, specifically citing those that have won prestigious awards like a Pulitzer Prize.

All signals are described with more detail here: https://lnkd.in/gaJB2snT

